      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When the delivery team arrives at Jhansi, the first step is a daylight verification against the original inventory bilty. Each pallet and container is cross‑checked with the signed bilty, confirming quantity, condition, and item codes.</p>
<p>Any discrepancy is immediately logged and a photo is taken for the audit trail. This early check prevents costly returns and ensures the client sees the exact goods they paid for.</p>

<p>Once verification is complete, the uncrating process begins. Workers use the designated lifting equipment to safely transfer items from pallets to the staging area. All fragile or high‑value pieces are handled by trained personnel wearing protective gloves and using padded mats. The team follows the “first in, first out” rule to maintain inventory integrity.</p>

<p>The next critical phase is testing. Electrical and mechanical items—such as HVAC units, kitchen appliances, and electronic panels—are plugged into a temporary power source under controlled conditions. A qualified technician runs a full diagnostics checklist, recording voltage levels, motor performance, and any audible anomalies.</p>
<p>Mechanical items like lifts or conveyors are operated at low speed to confirm smooth movement before full deployment. All test results are entered into the client’s system and a signed test sheet is attached to the delivery file.</p>

<p>With testing complete, the focus shifts to furniture placement. Each piece is positioned according to the floor plan, using a laser level to ensure alignment with walls and doorways. Furniture is cleaned with a microfiber wipe to remove dust and packaging residue.</p>
<p>The team also checks for proper assembly—hinges, screws, and brackets are tightened to manufacturer specifications. This meticulous placement guarantees that the client’s space looks ready for immediate use.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Finally, packing debris is removed swiftly.</p>
